exibility for higher-scoring patterns\n\nReason:\nPassing is the better choice. Chi W6 would expose another meld, making my hand fully melded with limited scoring potential (likely only Dragon Pung = 2 points, below the 8-point minimum). By passing, I maintain flexibility and have a clearer path to winning with B6 (1 tile remaining unshown), while keeping the hand structure that could score more points. The exposed melds already limit my scoring options, so preserving concealment where possible is strategic.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
